  "id": "USN-9146-1",
  "summary": "privoxy vulnerabilities",
  "details": "Joshua Rogers discovered that Privoxy incorrectly handled memory\nallocation, leading to a memory leak. An attacker could possibly use this\nissue to cause Privoxy to consume excessive resources, leading to a denial\nof service. (CVE-2021-44540)\n\nArtem Ivanov discovered that Privoxy did not properly encode template names\nin error pages. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to perform\ncross-site scripting attacks. (CVE-2021-44543)",
